{"id": "13364", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=13364", "title": "Green Cove Springs", "text": "Green Cove Springs is a city in the First Coast.\nGet in.\nUS 17 is primarily three lanes in each direction between Green Cove Springs and I-295 at Orange Park.\nJacksonville International Airport is the closest commercial airfield. The closest Amtrak stations are in Jacksonville and Palatka.\nGet around.\nYou'll need a car to get around. Orange Avenue (US 17) is the main north\u2013south route and has two lanes in each direction for its entire length through town.\nSee.\nA public pier at the end of Walnut Street extends into the St. Johns River, offering picturesque views of the waterfront.\nSpring Park, located on the river between Walnut Street and Spring Street, offers short paths for a stroll and a children's playground.\nDo.\nThe Clay Theatre, on Walnut Street at US 17/Orange Avenue, screens a couple of first-run features nightly and on Saturday and Sunday afternoons.\nSleep.\nThe closest hotels and motels are in Orange Park, a roughly 20-minute drive north on U.S. 17."}
